From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Aleksei Sviridkin <f@lex.la>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 22:02:57 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] net: accept phy-mode "sgmii-2500" as 2500base-x

NXP device trees describe a 2.5G SerDes link without in-band
autonegotiation as "sgmii-2500", which is what mainline calls
2500base-x. Parse the string as PHY_INTERFACE_MODE_2500BASEX instead of
carrying a separate interface mode, so existing device trees keep
working and phy_interface_t keeps mainline numbering.

Suggested-by: Vladimir Oltean <vladimir.oltean@nxp.com>
Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Aleksei Sviridkin <f@lex.la>
---
 Documentation/devicetree/bindings/net/ethernet-controller.yaml | 1 +
 drivers/base/property.c                                        | 4 ++++
 net/core/of_net.c                                              | 6 ++++++
 3 files changed, 11 insertions(+)

--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/net/ethernet-controller.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/net/ethernet-controller.yaml
@@ -42,6 +42,7 @@ properties:
       - mii-lite
       - gmii
       - sgmii
+      - sgmii-2500
       - psgmii
       - qsgmii
       - qusgmii
--- a/drivers/base/property.c
+++ b/drivers/base/property.c
@@ -1023,6 +1023,10 @@ int fwnode_get_phy_mode(const struct fwn
 		if (!strcasecmp(pm, phy_modes(i)))
 			return i;
 
+	/* NXP device trees name 2500base-x this way */
+	if (!strcasecmp(pm, "sgmii-2500"))
+		return PHY_INTERFACE_MODE_2500BASEX;
+
 	return -ENODEV;
 }
 EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(fwnode_get_phy_mode);
--- a/net/core/of_net.c
+++ b/net/core/of_net.c
@@ -43,6 +43,12 @@ int of_get_phy_mode(struct device_node *
 			return 0;
 		}
 
+	/* NXP device trees name 2500base-x this way */
+	if (!strcasecmp(pm, "sgmii-2500")) {
+		*interface = PHY_INTERFACE_MODE_2500BASEX;
+		return 0;
+	}
+
 	return -ENODEV;
 }
 EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(of_get_phy_mode);
